WEBVTT

00:00:02.189 --> 00:00:08.490
<v Sarah Okafor>Morning, everyone. Thursday the ninth. Can you hear me over that fan? Right, let's get the board straight.</v>

00:00:09.609 --> 00:00:16.960
<v Aisha Begum>Yeah, just about. Traffic on the ring road was dreadful. Spent longer looking at the factory than actually getting into it.</v>

00:00:17.280 --> 00:00:19.730
<v Jamie Brennan>Lovely view, though. Very desirable industrial estate.</v>

00:00:20.129 --> 00:00:27.129
<v Tomasz Nowak>Never mind that, it's the charity bake sale on Friday. Last time the cakes had gone before maintenance got there.</v>

00:00:28.170 --> 00:00:32.719
<v Sarah Okafor>A national scandal. Right, closed stuff first, then what we're actually taking away.</v>

00:00:35.039 --> 00:00:40.990
<v Jamie Brennan>I already swapped the filter on the MV01 yesterday. That's finished, not another one for today's list.</v>

00:00:43.380 --> 00:00:44.579
<v Sarah Okafor>Yep, closed. Cheers.</v>

00:00:46.060 --> 00:00:50.259
<v Tomasz Nowak>And I finished the repair on the IM3 last night. All done.</v>

00:00:51.299 --> 00:00:55.850
<v Priya Raman>Ah, good. I was looking at the old entry on the board, then.</v>

00:00:57.500 --> 00:01:05.549
<v Tomasz Nowak>Also, noticed the main conveyor was running a bit warm on nights but it settled down. Just an observation, nothing outstanding from that.</v>

00:01:06.040 --> 00:01:09.540
<v Aisha Begum>Right, so that's a nights note, not a fresh job.</v>

00:01:10.969 --> 00:01:21.469
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Same sort of note from me: noticed the Main Outfeed Conveyor was running a bit warm on nights but it settled down. No ongoing issue to put on the list.</v>

00:01:23.560 --> 00:01:27.060
<v Sarah Okafor>Okay, both observations only. Not turning either into an action.</v>

00:01:28.599 --> 00:01:35.599
<v Priya Raman>Mine hasn't moved, I'm afraid. Still waiting on parts for the GT2 bearing, nothing we can do until they arrive.</v>

00:01:37.030 --> 00:01:41.230
<v Jamie Brennan>Yeah, nothing in stores for that yet. Still blocked, not ready work.</v>

00:01:42.829 --> 00:01:46.329
<v Sarah Okafor>Understood. Leave that blocked. Let's take the safety-critical one first.</v>

00:01:47.049 --> 00:01:55.799
<v Sarah Okafor>Tomasz Nowak, can you go to Harbour Road to pick up the replacement parts for the Compressed Air Dryer? That one's safety critical, straight away.</v>

00:01:57.670 --> 00:02:04.319
<v Tomasz Nowak>Yeah, I'll go to Harbour Road and pick up the replacement parts for the Compressed Air Dryer straight away.</v>

00:02:06.519 --> 00:02:10.719
<v Jamie Brennan>That's collection only on this entry, yeah? Not fitting them as well?</v>

00:02:11.389 --> 00:02:15.240
<v Sarah Okafor>Correct, just the collection. We're not adding a fitting job here.</v>

00:02:16.830 --> 00:02:18.229
<v Tomasz Nowak>Fine, understood. Collection's mine.</v>

00:02:19.150 --> 00:02:26.500
<v Sarah Okafor>And Tomasz Nowak, can you run a function test on the line 1 mould temp next Tuesday? Fairly important, that one.</v>

00:02:28.300 --> 00:02:34.599
<v Tomasz Nowak>Yep, I'll run a function test on the line 1 mould temp next Tuesday. Fairly important, got it.</v>

00:02:37.020 --> 00:02:41.919
<v Aisha Begum>Sorry, you clipped a bit there. Was that a function test, not another repair?</v>

00:02:42.439 --> 00:02:46.639
<v Sarah Okafor>Function test on the line 1 mould temp, yes. That's the action.</v>

00:02:47.789 --> 00:02:49.889
<v Tomasz Nowak>Yeah, that's what I've got down.</v>

00:02:51.159 --> 00:02:59.210
<v Tomasz Nowak>While I'm on, I'll do the pre-use checks on the Forklift Fleet next week. That's holding production up so it needs doing first.</v>

00:03:00.319 --> 00:03:05.219
<v Sarah Okafor>Thanks, Tomasz Nowak. Forklift Fleet pre-use checks next week, first priority for that work.</v>

00:03:06.639 --> 00:03:12.240
<v Tomasz Nowak>Yeah, next week for those. Not saying they jump ahead of the safety-critical collection straight away.</v>

00:03:14.550 --> 00:03:16.650
<v Aisha Begum>Yep, different windows. That makes sense.</v>

00:03:18.009 --> 00:03:25.009
<v Fiona Doyle>Um, I'll do the lock-out tag-out sign-off on the line 1 TCU by 11am. I'll drop everything for that one.</v>

00:03:25.759 --> 00:03:29.960
<v Sarah Okafor>Thanks, Fi. Yes, drop everything for that one. That's the urgent sign-off.</v>

00:03:31.500 --> 00:03:35.000
<v Fiona Doyle>Understood. The line 1 TCU sign-off is mine, by 11am.</v>

00:03:36.439 --> 00:03:37.840
<v Priya Raman>Right. That's clear, cheers.</v>

00:03:40.229 --> 00:03:45.479
<v Fiona Doyle>And I'll send the shift handover report round today at 2pm. Low priority, that one.</v>

00:03:45.849 --> 00:03:49.000
<v Sarah Okafor>Okay, Fiona, report round today at 2pm, low priority.</v>

00:03:51.060 --> 00:03:54.909
<v Fiona Doyle>Yeah, separate from the sign-off. The report isn't the drop-everything job.</v>

00:03:56.889 --> 00:04:04.240
<v Sarah Okafor>Jamie Brennan, can you replace the seals on the Main Water Isolation Valve tomorrow morning? It matters but it's not urgent.</v>

00:04:05.060 --> 00:04:11.710
<v Jamie Brennan>Sorry, no, I can't take that one. I'm tied up in stores, so I can't commit to the seals.</v>

00:04:12.590 --> 00:04:21.339
<v Sarah Okafor>Okay. Olumide Adeyemi, can you take that instead: replace the seals on the Main Water Isolation Valve tomorrow morning? It matters but it's not urgent.</v>

00:04:23.470 --> 00:04:29.069
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Yeah, I'll take it. I'll replace the seals on the Main Water Isolation Valve tomorrow morning.</v>

00:04:29.529 --> 00:04:33.379
<v Jamie Brennan>Thanks. Just making sure it isn't still against me as well.</v>

00:04:34.990 --> 00:04:38.490
<v Olumide Adeyemi>No, Main Water Isolation Valve seals are with me now.</v>

00:04:40.259 --> 00:04:46.560
<v Sarah Okafor>Olumide Adeyemi, can you also do a site visit at Tollgate Water Treatment Works with the contractor tomorrow?</v>

00:04:48.629 --> 00:04:53.879
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Yes, I'll do the site visit at Tollgate Water Treatment Works with the contractor tomorrow.</v>

00:04:55.350 --> 00:04:58.850
<v Fiona Doyle>That's alongside the seals tomorrow morning. You're happy taking both?</v>

00:04:59.459 --> 00:05:03.310
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Yeah, those two are manageable. No clash on what I've got.</v>

00:05:04.680 --> 00:05:09.230
<v Sarah Okafor>Right, I'll update the risk assessment for work on the dryer on Friday.</v>

00:05:10.430 --> 00:05:15.329
<v Aisha Begum>Thanks, Saz. The risk assessment for work on the dryer, on Friday. Got that.</v>

00:05:16.139 --> 00:05:17.540
<v Sarah Okafor>Yep, that one's mine.</v>

00:05:19.889 --> 00:05:25.490
<v Fiona Doyle>Olumide Adeyemi, can you swap the filter on the water booster by 11am? It's low priority.</v>

00:05:27.889 --> 00:05:36.290
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Sorry, I can't take the water booster by 11am. Haven't got the capacity this morning. Tomorrow's two are fine, but not that as well.</v>

00:05:37.810 --> 00:05:44.459
<v Fiona Doyle>Okay. Sarah, can you take it instead? Swap the filter on the water booster by 11am. Still low priority.</v>

00:05:45.050 --> 00:05:50.300
<v Sarah Okafor>Yeah, I'll take that instead. I'll swap the filter on the water booster by 11am.</v>

00:05:51.120 --> 00:05:56.370
<v Priya Raman>Sorry, talking over you—low priority, but still by 11am? Just checking I've heard that right.</v>

00:05:57.379 --> 00:06:03.680
<v Sarah Okafor>That's right. Low priority, but the due time is still by 11am. I'm accepting it on that basis.</v>

00:06:04.389 --> 00:06:09.290
<v Jamie Brennan>And that's separate from the MV01 filter I mentioned. Mine was yesterday and finished.</v>

00:06:09.720 --> 00:06:11.819
<v Sarah Okafor>Exactly. No duplicate job for yours.</v>

00:06:13.220 --> 00:06:18.120
<v Tomasz Nowak>Good. I can cope with two filter names, but apparently not two cake queues.</v>

00:06:19.279 --> 00:06:24.180
<v Aisha Begum>You'd still pick the slower queue. Same skill I've got on the ring road.</v>

00:06:25.490 --> 00:06:32.490
<v Fiona Doyle>Just to close mine out: urgent line 1 TCU sign-off by 11am, low-priority handover report today at 2pm. Both accepted.</v>

00:06:34.060 --> 00:06:37.209
<v Sarah Okafor>Yep, that's exactly how we've got them. Nothing extra.</v>

00:06:38.449 --> 00:06:42.649
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Sound. Teams actually behaved this morning. Usually I miss every third word.</v>

00:06:44.439 --> 00:06:47.240
<v Priya Raman>Don't tempt it. We've nearly made it through.</v>

00:06:47.670 --> 00:06:52.220
<v Sarah Okafor>Right, we're agreed. Closed items stay closed, parts blocker stays blocked. Thanks, everyone.</v>
